Hexalith.Agents Story 5.4 is blocked on the Platform-owned `EXT-SECRETS-1` record. The owning repository is still `TBD` in [the dependency register](https://github.com/Hexalith/Hexalith.Agents/blob/main/_bmad-output/planning-artifacts/external-dependency-register.md#ext-secrets-1--platform-secret-resolution). This issue requests the Platform Maintainer's repository and complete commitment; the Story 5.4 HMAC subset alone cannot make the broader record Available.

For Story 5.4, the accepted trusted-envelope profile must fix issuer, audience, HMAC-SHA-256 AD-30 canonical bytes, constant-time verification, **numeric** maximum tag lifetime, clock skew, rotation overlap, command retry/recovery horizon, and replay retention at least the greater of lifetime + skew + overlap and recovery horizon. It must define active/revoked key state, routine rotation, emergency revocation and redispatch with a new nonce, retained digest versions, issuer-wide nonce uniqueness, and the reserved-system HMAC security-observation digest. The non-public replay registrar must be restricted to the exact replay stream/event and unavailable to public, Workflow, and target-handler paths.

The complete record also requires versioned Provider, KEK/DEK, export/manifest, migration capability, decision-trust, and deletion-batch signing/revocation custody and outcome lookup as written in the register, including its current v23 extensions. Please name the independent decision-approval issuer; platform custody must not mint approval evidence.

For register acceptance, please reply with:
- the Platform Maintainer's acceptance of the complete contract, selected owning repository, and final public/typed members;
- one immutable package version or full commit covering the complete target;
- an accepted target integration date;
- the exact executable clean-checkout compatibility command and live Level 4 evidence for all required custody, replay, rotation/revocation, signing, lookup, and denied-access cases, with Level 5 requirements acknowledged.

Agents will keep `EXT-SECRETS-1` Uncommitted until all fields are accepted. A passing HMAC-only test is partial evidence, not record availability.

Hexalith.Agents Story 5.4 is blocked on the Platform-owned `EXT-HOST-1` record. See [the full current contract and v21/v23 extensions](https://github.com/Hexalith/Hexalith.Agents/blob/main/_bmad-output/planning-artifacts/external-dependency-register.md#ext-host-1--platform-owned-agents-host-composition). The historical `a66cdf346e521ad147f442b686f301f0f59c525c` target and `./eng/verify-agents-host.sh` prove only the earlier AppHost scaffold/build boundary; the script explicitly says live Agents composition remains future work. They are not a current acceptance target or availability command.

Story 5.4 requires a Platform-owned, replicated, durable, content-free `security-audit-spool`: deterministic observation accepted before denial is reported; exact-id lookup/acknowledgement; pending retention through EventStore/replay outage; a least-privilege recovery worker that can append only the computed `SecurityEventLog(RoutingTenantId, UtcDay)` event/stream; and fail-closed ingress/readiness if spool or restricted credentials are unavailable. The non-public replay credential must conditionally append only the reserved-system `TrustedEnvelopeReplay` event/stream and be inaccessible to public, human, Workflow, target-handler, or general dispatcher paths. Host composition must wire Agents DomainService/UI with EventStore, Conversations, Parties, Tenants, secrets, identity, Workflow, provider/safety adapters, health, telemetry, and the full later protection, migration, governance, and deletion contracts in the register.

For register acceptance, please reply with:
- Platform Maintainer acceptance of the **complete expanded** artifact and Levels 4 and 5 evidence;
- one immutable full commit covering it;
- an accepted target integration date;
- the exact executable clean-checkout compatibility command with live Level 4 evidence for spool fail-closed/recovery/ACL, host composition, FR-34 protection attestation, migration/write fences, and current v21/v23 guard/protection-owner races.

A Story 5.4-only spool or the historical build verifier is partial evidence, not `EXT-HOST-1` availability. The Agents register will remain Uncommitted until every current commitment field is accepted.
